<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7565"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:sugar@mhtc.net" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Mcattitude<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Mcattitude<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 11:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Possible new BTK package <BR> <BR> <BR>By Kim Setty <BR>KWCH 12 Eyewitness News <BR>Wednesday, February 16, 2005 <BR> <BR>   <BR>Wichita police are investigating a possible new communication from BTK---a mailing to KSAS-TV Wednesday morning. <BR> <BR>Two employees from Fox Kansas going through the mail discovered it, which contains items that may be from BTK. <BR> <BR>At police request, Eyewitness News is not revealing the contents. <BR> <BR>Workers called police, who took it as evidence. <BR> <BR>Investigators are looking over the mailing to determine whether it is from BTK. <BR> <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7565-->
<!--Post: 7586--><!--Time: 1108589088-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7586"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:nugzter@yahoo.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Nugzter<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nugzter<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 1:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I wonder what will be said about new package &#40;16FEB&#41; in the report. If the new letter is released in full then we will know BTK is calling the shots.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7586-->
<!--Post: 7602--><!--Time: 1108595590-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7602"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Sandy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Sandy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 3:13 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->He must be upset with KAKE for not giving out the information he wants to be known. Letter sent to &#34;Fox&#34; News. I wonder if it has anything to do with Nancy ? I was expecting something mailed for Valentines Day,he must be getting a bit slow?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7602-->
<!--Post: 7605--><!--Time: 1108596864-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7605"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 3:34 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Found this on Kansas.com: <BR>From:  Alice7_again   6:23 pm   <BR>To:  ALL   &#40;15 of 15&#41;   <BR>  <BR>  5978.15 in reply to 5978.13   <BR>  <BR>The letter was from P.J. Fox with the Fox affiliate address on it. It had many stamps on it and siad he wanted to start a new change by sending it to Fox instead of Kake.  <BR> <BR>My question is, could someone be charged with impeding an investigation if they took the info straight to a national news network so they would list ALL of the contents of the letters before the police put limits on it? <BR> <BR>Maybe his story would be out then, once and for all. <BR> <BR>  <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7605-->
<!--Post: 7610--><!--Time: 1108600555-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7610"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 4:35 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here are the latest news about the package/letter sent to kansas Fox Tv-station today. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1272122.html" target=_top>http://www.kake.com/home/headlines/1272122.html</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
